WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.702
-My next guest
is a Grammy-winning artist

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.905
and a judge on the new series
"Clash of the Cover Bands,"

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:10.376
which premieres tomorrow night
at 9:30 p.m. on E!

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.312
Here is Meghan Trainor!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:16.883
No way!
Come on!

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.352
Oh, I love you.
Hi, bud.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.619
-Hi!
-Thank you so much

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:22.989
for being on the show.
I appreciate it.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.390
-Oh, thank you for having me.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.524
Every time it's like
my first time ever.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:26.759
I love you.
-Oh, my God.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.160
You're the greatest.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.629
We have so many things I have
to discuss and talk about.

00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:34.700
You know where we have to start,
and this is the headlines --

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.068
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:39.873
This is a real headline
that was trending this week.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.709
Maybe yesterday?
"Meghan Trainor reveals

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:46.345
she and Daryl have two toilets

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:48.481
next to each other
in their bathroom."

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:53.186
That's all anyone could talk
about for the last three days.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.920
-Yeah.
Yeah, my mom's like,

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.889
"I wish there was song
attached to this."

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:59.425
[ Laughter ]
But there's not.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.227
I didn't know it was gonna
be such a big deal.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.896
That's why I casually
brought it up on a podcast.

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:07.333
But, yeah, when I --
We moved into this new house,

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.602
and, you know, you get up
all throughout the night

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.371
with a baby, and you got to pee.

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:14.607
And there's so many moments
where I was like, "Move!"

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.543
You know?
I was like, "I have to go."

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.977
-Yeah.
-And so when we moved to this

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.579
new house, I was like,
"I have an extra toilet.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:22.548
Can I just pop them
next to each other?"

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.384
And the plumber, like, giggled,
and I was like,

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.051
"I don't see
why you're laughing.

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:28.087
Like, just do it, get it done."

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:32.058
And they did it, and, like,
it's the best thing I ever did.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.592
-I have to show this
because you --

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:35.895
This is a "Tonight Show"
exclusive.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.397
You brought a photo
of your bathroom.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.333
-Yes.
Oh, yeah.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.268
-This is real.
Look at this.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.970
-This is real.
-All right, so wait.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.104
Now this is --
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:47.840
Meghan.
This is a --

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.076
This is a terrible --
This is a terrible idea.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.712
This is a terrible idea.
First of all, I don't even --

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.413
Should I ask?
Is it rude to ask?

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:56.349
Whose is whose?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.349 --> 00:02:00.453
-So, mine's -- I -- Mine's
the fancy one on the right.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:03.022
It, like, warms your butt,
and then the other one

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.792
on the left is right under the
air conditioning, so that's his.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.161
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.563
-That's so funny.
So, now are you gonna keep this,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.631
or are you going to change it?

00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:14.167
-You know how expensive
it would be to change that?

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.101
No, this is the best thing
about my house.

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:18.071
It's my favorite
part of the house.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.339
-Now it's legendary.
Now you got it.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.707
You have to do it now.
-Now it's really famous.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.409
I told my contractor,
I was like, "Did you hear?"

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.611
He's like,
"My sister told me the news."

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:28.147
I'm like, "You're famous."
-Yeah.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:31.150
I want to say congrats again.
I know we talked about this.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.453
"A Very Trainor Christmas"
came out.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:38.724
You have the deluxe version
coming out later this month.

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.426
I loved it.
I loved "Holidays"

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.394
with Earth, Wind and Fire,
was my jam.

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:43.696
-Yeah!
-That was great.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.499
-Thank you.
-I just -- I --

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:49.201
You know I love the holidays,
so this is, like, massive.

00:02:49.201 --> 00:02:50.470
So to come out with --

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:54.306
The deluxe edition has
how many new jams on this?

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:57.143
-Three new jams.
-Three new jams.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.978
I'm excited about this.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.981
We can call them jams right?
-Gems.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.883
-Oh, gems, of course.
Yes, gems.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.185
They're gems,
but they're also jams.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.386
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:10.289
I think you should come out --

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:13.192
you should come out
with an album of kid songs.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:15.761
-I think so, too.
That would be a great idea.

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.396
Plus, I'm sick of these
old nursery rhymes.

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:20.466
The lyrics are way too dark,
and they're annoying.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.834
So I want to do
a whole new batch of them.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.636
-Dark?
-They're dark.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.838
The lyrics are dark, if you
really think about some of them.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.073
Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:29.842
How is the baby?
-He's perfection.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.944
He's here somewhere,
but he's adorable.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:34.847
He's 8 months now.
He says, "Mama" and "Dada."

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.849
He doesn't know what it means,
but we just accept it.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.485
We're like, "It's me, mama."
So he's great.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.653
-"Mama."
-Yeah.

00:03:41.653 --> 00:03:44.289
-You just started him in music
class, which always cute.

00:03:44.289 --> 00:03:47.226
How is that going?
-It's great.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.228
That's another thing
that went pretty viral.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:52.998
But it's -- I got --
I'm like, "I got accepted."

00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:56.168
Hilary Duff started this
amazing music class

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:58.270
with a bunch of moms
that she's friends with.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:01.174
And I showed up, and I was,
like, trying to act really cool,

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.442
but I was dying inside
because there was, like,

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:06.412
Miss Mandy Moore
and Ashley Tisdale

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.314
and Hilary Duff,
and I'm just like -- [ Gasps ]

00:04:09.314 --> 00:04:11.818
"My dreams!"
-Are you --

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:14.453
I know you're a big
"Lizzy McGuire" fan, right?

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:16.088
-Huge.
-Me too.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:19.358
-Yeah, my alias at hotel names
would be Lizzy McGuire.

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:22.528
But my husband is an even bigger
Mandy Moore fan.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.763
She doesn't know this, though.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.932
But he named his hamster
Mandy Moore

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.333
when he was growing up.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.769
-Oh, my gosh.
He can't admit that to her.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.103
No, no, no, yeah.
But what --

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:33.106
-No.
-So all these --

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.942
Mandy Moore's kid and your kid
singing in same music class.

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:39.345
I know they're babies, but
it's got to sound pretty good.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.946
-Singing away.
-I'd buy it.

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:42.115
[ Laughter ]
I'd buy it.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:44.816
Yeah. I mean, come on.
How cute is that?

00:04:44.816 --> 00:04:46.218
-It would be adorable.

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:49.121
-I want to talk about
"Clash of the Cover Bands."

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:51.523
This is tomorrow night on E!
-Yeah!

00:04:51.523 --> 00:04:55.094
9:30, Wednesday.
9:30, on E!

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:58.097
I'm excited
because I'm producing this show.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.466
-You're a part of it.
-Yeah.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:04.103
I'm a major part of this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:07.006
I'm so excited that
you did this, because, you know,

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:10.776
I love -- we both love music,
and I do love cover bands.

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:12.512
So when someone
came up with this idea,

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:15.948
I go, "Oh, we got to do this."
We talked about cover bands

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.282
when you were on our show

00:05:17.282 --> 00:05:19.685
because your family
was in a cover band.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.054
Was it Island Fusion
or something?

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:24.890
-Yes, it was. This is
so embarrassing, but, yes.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.492
I was in a --
-I love the name.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:29.062
-I was in a band with family,
Island Fusion, and we'd do,

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:31.898
like, pop songs
and soca songs and funk.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.299
It was great.
-Yeah.

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.801
And now, doing this,
what was your experience like

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:37.503
being a judge on "Clash of --"

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:40.673
By the way, the winner gets
to come on "The Tonight Show."

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.342
-Whoo! And perform.
-And, yeah,

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:45.277
performing on the show.
It's a big deal.

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:47.379
I love --
-And money.

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:48.915
-And they get money.
Yeah, I mean,

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:51.284
this is a game-changer
for a lot of people, yeah.

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:54.086
-[ Laughs ]
-But I love --

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:57.490
We can't say who wins
or who our favorites are,

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:00.693
but there were some
knockout performances.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.928
-Yeah.
They were really unbelievable.

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:04.997
I know we had --
I remember we had a Cher

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:07.299
and Celine Dion and --
-Oh, that's right.

00:06:07.299 --> 00:06:10.302
-I remember, in the building,
people would come up

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:12.472
to my family and say,
"Oh, my God.

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:14.940
Did you hear that Cher is here?"
Like, they really

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.410
fooled everyone
in that building,

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.344
because they were so good.
-Yeah.

00:06:19.344 --> 00:06:23.048
What do you think is the key
to having a good cover band?

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:27.119
-I think not -- never thinking

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:30.156
that you're better
than the original icon.

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:32.958
And I also loved
a lot of the covers we had

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:34.694
when they would
stay in character.

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:36.061
Like, when we were
interviewing them

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:39.531
and asked them the questions,
they were, like, Bono

00:06:39.531 --> 00:06:40.933
or they were Celine Dion.
-Yes!

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.935
-And I was like,
"Oh, I love you," yeah.

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:45.438
-Isn't that great?
I remember seeing

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:49.242
a Beatles cover band years ago.
-Yes.

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.843
-And they all
just stayed in character.

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.945
And they're like, "Hey, John."
"What, Paul?"

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:56.682
He goes, "Right now, there's
$1 tequila shots at the bar."

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:57.916
And he's like --
They were, like,

00:06:57.916 --> 00:07:00.318
pitching discounts for booze
at the bar.

00:07:00.318 --> 00:07:03.622
I go, "You'd never seen John
and Paul ever do that."

00:07:03.622 --> 00:07:06.492
But they loved the Beatles
so much, and they were like --

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:08.694
It was just fun.
And I just --

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.829
-Yeah.
-I just thought this experience

00:07:10.829 --> 00:07:13.065
was so good.
If you love music,

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:16.501
if you love watching
these awesome battles play out,

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:17.803
it's definitely worth it.

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:21.073
By the way, I will say,
the Elton John is amazing.

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:23.576
-That -- Yeah,
that was one of my favorites.

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:25.978
His outfits are so good.
-Yeah.

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:28.080
And we also, like,
upped the game

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.017
once they came to our show,
with wardrobe and whatever

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:33.386
we could do to play it up.
-Oh, yeah.

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:35.187
-I think you're gonna love it,
and you're fantastic on it,

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:38.123
so thank you so much.
It's fun working with you, bud.

00:07:38.123 --> 00:07:39.892
-Thanks for thinking of me.
I love you!

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:42.561
[ Laughter ]
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:42.561 --> 00:07:44.430
Here's a peek at
"Clash of the Cover Bands."

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.698
Take a look at this.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:49.001
-That's Bono.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:51.670
Meghan, break it down for us.
What are the judges looking for?

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:54.040
-So, we're judging you
on vocal impressions.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.841
Do you sound like the icon?

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:57.009
Physical embodiment.

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.711
Do you move your body
like the icon?

00:07:59.711 --> 00:08:01.380
And, finally,
overall performance.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:05.184
Did we enjoy it?
And can I just say A-plus, plus.

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:09.989
Y'all are so tight as a band,
and, Sir Bono, I believe you.

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:11.457
You're incredible.

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:13.058
Your vocals
are actually amazing, too.

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:14.626
Like, you're doing
the right thing.

00:08:14.626 --> 00:08:17.029
You're doing a great job.
-Thank you.

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:21.033
-Esther, how you feeling?
-I felt very entertained.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.135
You know, Bono, you knocking it,
you rocking it.

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:26.839
But, you know,
U2 is a huge stadium band,

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:30.109
and I would like to see
everybody put it all out there.

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:31.677
You know what I'm saying?
With your movement.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.112
Just take it to the next level.

00:08:33.112 --> 00:08:35.214
[ Applause ]
-Thank you so much.

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:37.950
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.686
-We were talking --

00:08:40.686 --> 00:08:44.523
I also like the fact that, like,
these bands are also, like,

00:08:44.523 --> 00:08:46.959
that guy has seen U2 in concert,

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:48.894
like, over 100 times
or something.

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:51.196
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I think it was like 78 times

00:08:51.196 --> 00:08:53.766
or something beyond that.
It's crazy.

00:08:53.766 --> 00:08:55.201
-Studied the band,
every single move,

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.436
and when you see him, like --
the guy who's doing Chris Martin

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:59.638
in Coldplay, you're like
"This is just awesome."

00:08:59.638 --> 00:09:01.040
It's just so much fun to watch.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.209
-They worship them, and that was
the beautiful part, too.

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:06.745
Because, also, cover bands
don't get enough, like, credit.

00:09:06.745 --> 00:09:08.414
They don't.
They work so hard,

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:11.117
and it's their entire life,
it's their passion.

00:09:11.117 --> 00:09:13.386
And, like, finally,
you've given them a place

00:09:13.386 --> 00:09:16.522
to shine, and I'm so honored
to be part of it.

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:18.190
-Aw, I love you.
Meghan Trainor, everybody!

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.591
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:19.591 --> 00:09:22.528
"Clash of the Cover Bands"
premieres tomorrow night on E!

